// Expected: a1 at one session and at two (GitHub issue #33).
//
// Bob uses x only through Carol: he relays it to her under a guard, she
// returns HASH(x) under a guard, and Bob hashes that. Sanity accepts the
// query because the guarded relay carries whatever Bob received, so Bob's x
// reaches Carol's digest. The attacker replaces x at Bob's unguarded receive
// with nil. Bob relays nil, Carol returns HASH(nil) and Bob uses it: a1. The
// judge once followed only Bob's own assignments. It stopped at Carol's digest,
// found no use and reported a0. A recipient with no direct use of a value now
// has its uses found as sanity finds them, through other principals'
// computations. A recipient that uses the value directly keeps only those uses
// (spore_ns_pk.vp). auth_use_through_checked_relay.vp is the counterweight,
// where the relayed use never runs.
attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	generates x
]

Alice -> Bob: x

Bob -> Carol: [x]

principal Carol[
	digest = HASH(x)
]

Carol -> Bob: [digest]

principal Bob[
	result = HASH(digest)
]

queries[
	authentication? Alice -> Bob: x
]
